==Strategy==
:'''Sniper the Cat, [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Recruit]] and [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]] do more harm than good in all strategies. They will desync the Manic King Dragons and thereby make it more difficult to kill them.'''

[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] is an easily accessible unit who outranges and chips the Manic King Dragons. Never go below a sustainable cash amount, and stack [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Flying Cat]] to take out the Otta-smack-u waves. [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera]] and a (few) well-timed [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cats]] will eventually kill the Manic King Dragon Cats. It is unwise to attempt to beat this stage without Awakened Bahamut or [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless]] ubers.

When the Manic King Dragon Cats die, let Awakened Bahamut die, and rush the enemy base with [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] as a shield for him to quickly take out the base before another Otta-smack-u wave comes to disrupt everything. If [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] is not spawned as often as possible, peons might push through because of the Otta-smack-us and the Manic King Dragons will get close and begin damaging your long-ranged attacker(s).

This stage is an endurance match, and you must cycle Awakened Bahamut along with Manic Flying or another spammable DPS unit to eventually break down the Manic King Dragon stacks that appear as you damage the base.

This stage can be rushed using Awakened Bahamut alongside other rushers such as [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Yukimura]] or [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]] with Attack UP [[Cat Combo|Cat Combos]] to rush down the enemy base before the Manic King Dragons can stack up and kill them.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] - Very cheap and stackable, extremely helpful for taking out the Otta waves.
*[[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Flying]] - Similar to Cameraman, albeit noticeably more expensive. Watch your money when using it, and never send it out unless it would be out of the Manic Dragons' range when dealing with the Ottas.
*[[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Legs]] - Crazed Sexy Legs can be useful, but true form is ideal, as the higher wave level allows it to snipe the Manic Dragons at the back while there are Ottas in front of them serving as stepping stones.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - At level 40, Courier Cat can withstand at least 6 attacks from the Manic King Dragons without taking knockback, providing gradual chip damage over time, eventually killing the dragons without having to spend too much money.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] - A natural pick for this stage, Cyberpunk is actually able to '''outrange''' the manic King Dragons and provide support with his slow and additional chip damage. However, he is quite fragile, so protect him from the Otta waves and you'll be fine.
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] - Although there are no aliens in this stage, Seafarer's raw stats are enough to help out a ton in this stage with dealing with the Otta waves.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] - Similar usage to Seafarer, but he has higher health and stats at the cost of being more expensive and slower.
*[[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera]] and [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed M. Titan]] - Very tanky units that can walk right up to the Manic Dragons with a clear path and deal chip damage. Don't expect them to survive for too long during an Otta wave, however, as the Ottas will shred their HP.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] - A cheap unit that does an absurdly high amount of damage for their cost, Can Can is a great unit that can be used to dispose of the Ottas quickly. With [[Talents|talents]], Can Can is actually able to get double the money if they land the finishing blow on an Otta, giving you substantially more money and makes saving for the next wave a lot easier.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] - A cheap unit that is very useful in killing the starting Mooths and can rush into the Otta-smack-us, dealing some nice damage. However, he may prove rather inconsistent for the Dragons due to not having enough endurance or range to reach them and might instead just get juggled to death.
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]] - Since most of the enemies here are traitless, Haniwa makes stalling these enemies extremely easy as it takes 1/4 the damage a unit would normally take.

==='''Recommended Ubers/Legend Rares'''===
*Rusher-class Ubers such as [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'arktanyan]], [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]], [[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru]] and [[Blanka (Uber Rare Cat)|Blanka]] can help in rushing the Otter waves, and potentially can chip the Manic King Dragons if timed correctly. If they do not rush first and foremost, testing your timing by trying to cheese this stage is a viable option, although they help no matter what you bring them for. However, before determining if your unit is viable as a rusher, check their speed; having roughly 40 speed and most ideally 50+ is enough. Notice a sufficiently upgraded [[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]] can quickly dispatch the Otter waves and pause the advancement of the Dragons without the need of exact timing.
**Beware the possibility of them desyncing the Manic King Dragons! While they help for both chipping them and the Otters, they might also increase the rate at which the Dragons attack <u>if you are not careful enough</u>! Focus on only spawning these types of units during the Otter waves!
**Issun Boshi's first form might be preferred thanks to it basically being an anti-Traitless Fishman Cat, along with having Area Attack.
*[[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]], [[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]], and other such tankers with short recharge times may potentially bring the danger of the Otta-smack-u waves down as well, but depending on their levels, they may not last as long as you may want. To fix this problem, it's recommended that you increase their level to or above 30 if possible. '''Do NOT use tankers with long recharge time here! For the time after they have died, they will functionally be a waste of a slot and useless!'''
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Super Galaxy Cosmo]], [[Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Balalan Pasalan]] and [[Asiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Assassinlan Pasalan]] are able to actually '''outrange''' the Manic King Dragons, allowing for them to safely provide respite from/damage the Manic King Dragons over time. However, each has a high cost, so protect them well! This especially matters with the Pasalans, who have pitiful health and excessively long recharge times, meaning you will likely '''<u>NOT</u>''' get another if you let one of them die!
**Because of his speed, Super Galaxy Cosmo is a unit you must be careful with; with the default [[Cat Cannon]] or Breakerblast, he will rush forward into the Manic King Dragons and die. Therefore, choose the Thunderbolt or Slow Beam Cannon to use instead.**
*[[Izanami of Dusk (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanami of Eventide]] deals insane damage to Traitless enemies and has enough health to tank the Manic King Dragons for a while. Her spirit can also act as a one-time burst of damage to kill a horde of Otta-smack-us and possibly rip a chunk out of the Dragons if she's close enough.

